  <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="section-new-here">
    <h2 class="section-heading" id="section-new-here">Never Done This Before?</h2>
    <p class="section-sub">Most people who walk into our room have never set foot on a stage in their lives. Honestly, that's exactly who these nights are for. No theater background, no witty comebacks needed. If you're wondering how to start, here's the path we'd nudge a friend down:</p>

    <ol class="about-ladder">
      <li>
        <span class="about-ladder-step">1</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Drop into Whimsical Wednesday</strong>
          <p>Our weekly flagship jam. You don't have to perform. You just show up after work, play low-stakes group circle games, laugh at absurd imaginary gifts, and see what improv actually feels like in a room where nobody is judging you.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="about-ladder-step">2</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Make friends with the stage</strong>
          <p>When you're ready to do a little more than watch from the sidelines. Quick, supported two-person scenes with zero pressure — we keep things moving fast, and you can step onto the stage or take a seat whenever you feel like it.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="about-ladder-step">3</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Take Improv 101: How Not to Panic on Stage</strong>
          <p>A weekend crash course designed specifically around stage fright. We build up in tiny, manageable steps — learning how to trust your instincts, silence the inner critic, and discover the genuine joy of messing up.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="about-ladder-step">4</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Go down the rabbit hole</strong>
          <p>Once you're hooked: try musical improv (making up songs from scratch even if you think you can't sing), join our multi-week storytelling intensives, or dive into competitive formats like TheatreSports™ and PowerPoint Roulette.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>

